================================================================================================
G1 -- the REAL case: `dae9d2b5-half-param` rung 1, under each metric
================================================================================================

intended rung: half(g, i) = nth(split_h(#0), #1)   arity 2
retained programs sleep is fed:
  half-w0      nth(split_h(input), 0)
  half-w1      nth(split_h(input), 0)
  half-e0      nth(split_h(input), 1)
  half-e1      nth(split_h(input), 1)

  CompressionMetric (flat, THE DEFAULT)
    kept 2: abs0(arity 1), abs1(arity 1)
    final DL 14.0   recovers `half`: False

  TwoPartMDL (anti-bloat)
    kept 0: 
    final DL 20.0   recovers `half`: False

================================================================================================
G2 -- the greedy TRAJECTORY: what is on offer at each round, under the default metric
================================================================================================

  round 0: corpus = ['nth(split_h(input), 0)', 'nth(split_h(input), 0)', 'nth(split_h(input), 1)', 'nth(split_h(input), 1)']
      offered: arity 1  nth(split_h(#0), 0)
      offered: arity 1  nth(split_h(#0), 1)
      offered: arity 2  nth(split_h(#0), #1)   <-- the intended `half`
      the arity-2 generalisation is ON OFFER; selector takes: nth(split_h(#0), 0)

  round 1: corpus = ['abs0(input)', 'abs0(input)', 'nth(split_h(input), 1)', 'nth(split_h(input), 1)']
      offered: arity 1  abs0(#0)
      offered: arity 1  nth(split_h(#0), 1)
      the arity-2 generalisation is GONE; selector takes: nth(split_h(#0), 1)

  round 2: corpus = ['abs0(input)', 'abs0(input)', 'abs1(input)', 'abs1(input)']
      offered: arity 1  abs0(#0)
      offered: arity 1  abs1(#0)
      selector: nothing improves DL -- loop ends

  ^ If the generalisation is ON OFFER at round 0 but GONE by round 1, it was not weighed and
    rejected on the merits -- the first mint's REWRITE destroyed the pair it is derived from.

================================================================================================
G3 -- the END STATES, priced directly: does greedy reach the DL-minimum?
================================================================================================

  CompressionMetric (flat, THE DEFAULT)
    do nothing                         DL     20.0  (library    4.0 + programs   16.0)
    SPECIALISE (what greedy did)       DL     14.0  (library    6.0 + programs    8.0)
    GENERALISE (the intended `half`)   DL     17.0  (library    5.0 + programs   12.0)
    BOTH                               DL     15.0  (library    7.0 + programs    8.0)
    -> DL-minimal end state: SPECIALISE (what greedy did) (14.0)

  TwoPartMDL (anti-bloat)
    do nothing                         DL     20.0  (library    4.0 + programs   16.0)
    SPECIALISE (what greedy did)       DL     22.0  (library   14.0 + programs    8.0)
    GENERALISE (the intended `half`)   DL     21.0  (library    9.0 + programs   12.0)
    BOTH                               DL     27.0  (library   19.0 + programs    8.0)
    -> DL-minimal end state: do nothing (20.0)

